  "experimentId": "frontline-five-slot-tuning-v1",
  "status": "experimental",
  "hypothesis": "Five-slot tuning (DECISIONS #171): phase 2 measured the fabricator dominant on both seed sets (bulwark-vs-fabricator -0.833/-0.833, fabricator-vs-striker +0.778/+0.667 toward the fabricator) and attributed the overshoot to FIVE SLOTS via the pair structure. Three registered single-lever variants are measured against the rig control on the three fabricator-involving pairs (bulwark-vs-striker cells cannot change bytes under a five-slot variant and are not re-run). Pre-registered gates: T1 the control replicates phase 2 (bulwark-vs-fabricator within 0.25 of -0.833); T2 at least one variant brings BOTH cross-class fabricator edges to |payoff| <= 0.40, with the [0.15, 0.40] band aspirational -- the striker-side edge is population-capped by arc-light's measured -1.00 against fabricators on EVERY arm including keel (a lineage limit, not a mechanism fact; disclosed, not gated); T3 do-no-harm on each variant arm: fabricator-mirror draw rate and capped-match share must not exceed the control arm's by more than 0.05, and pooled leader-extends must not fall below 0.45x the control arm's. SELECTION RULE (registered to forbid knob-shopping): adopt the variant minimizing max(|bulwark-vs-fabricator payoff|, |fabricator-vs-striker payoff|) among those passing T3; ties prefer a variant keeping five slots (the owner's numbers-class identity ruling), then prefer boom (schedule-only, smallest behavioral surface). If no variant passes T2, adopt nothing and design composite arms in a fresh pre-registration. Disclosures: single-lever arms only; the wave-4 fabricator doctrines were authored against the full 60/180/300/420 schedule, so a bot that hardcoded those unlocks misplays boom/trim mildly (both fabricator lineages claimed contract-driven slot reading; measured, not assumed); the volley and shell are untouched per the slate; leave-one-skill-out arms remain deferred.",
